<p>WhereIsTheBin helps people in Kerala find public bins and authorised waste facilities near them, in English and Malayalam. It is a community information service. We do not collect, process or dispose of waste ourselves.</p>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Find.</strong> Search for a place or share your location to see nearby places.</li>
  <li><strong>Check.</strong> Every place shows what it accepts and when it was last verified. A place that has not been checked for more than 180 days is marked as possibly out of date.</li>
  <li><strong>Walk there.</strong> Get walking directions without leaving the site.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
<p>People in the community add places. A new place stays hidden until a moderator reviews it. Moderators can approve a place, reject it with a reason, correct its details, or archive it. Anyone with an account can report a problem with a place, such as a bin that is full, damaged, missing or in the wrong location, and moderators review each report. Every moderator action is recorded in an audit log.</p>

<h2>What to expect</h2>
<p>Information can be wrong or out of date. A bin may be full, moved or closed, and some facilities accept only certain materials or limit who can use them. Please check the signs on site. WhereIsTheBin cannot arrange waste collection or promise that a place will accept your waste. Walking directions are only a guide: watch the traffic and follow local signs.</p>

<h2>Contributing</h2>
<p>You are welcome to add public bins and facilities you know about, and to report problems you see. Please:</p>
<ul>
  <li>add only places that are open to the public or that publish their services, not private homes;</li>
  <li>do not write personal information, such as phone numbers or house addresses of individuals, in notes;</li>
  <li>send reports only for real problems.</li>
</ul>
<p>We may restrict accounts that repeatedly submit false or harmful information.</p>

<h2>Map data and credits</h2>
<p>Map data © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors. Place search uses Nominatim, walking routes use OSRM on servers run by FOSSGIS (OpenStreetMap Germany), and the map is drawn with Leaflet. We currently use free public services, which may change or limit use.</p>

<h2>Language</h2>
<p>The site is available in English and Malayalam. If you notice a wording mistake, please tell us.</p>